data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":1039,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0548a1ebceca9325016b03228ba99487d1be2d9496adf3adfc","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"ash-1\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"The requested effect is conservative aggregation of compatible fractional supplies, not gathering, transfer, extraction or food processing. No supplied implemented interface provides it. Two validated 0.7-unit bark stacks can supply 1.0 unit and leave 0.4 units without producing material. Their full ownership, accessibility and compatibility must be checked at execution; the omitted second stack cannot be presumed invalid or available.\",\"specification\":\"Implement material-stack-combine@1 with interface material-stack-combine. Public schema: {operation:'combine', sourceIds:string[2..16], expectedVersions?:object}; return {status, outputId, quantityTenths, componentLots, costs, failureReason}. Shared references use existing actor/item IDs, resource IDs, world coordinates, interaction reach 0.65, dt=1 and integer quantityTenths. Requires individual mastery, a living actor, at least two distinct unlocked owned stacks, sufficient energy, and actual accessible material. Carried items are accessible; owned ground items must each be within interaction reach with unobstructed contact. Ownership alone does not imply proximity. No tool or additional material is required.\\nCompatibility: use the same canonical resource and unit definition, with actual material form and intrinsic properties satisfying the same downstream requirements. Compare represented processing profiles, not names alone. Reject incompatible solid/fines forms, incompatible physical processing states, or different intrinsic unit masses; never convert bark-fines into bark. Different origins and histories are allowed but remain separate component lots. Resolve the two named bark stacks from full retained state before deciding compatibility.\\nState: each combined item has an ordinary addressable item ID and a component-lot ledger preserving original IDs, quantity, mass, composition, fuel, moisture, age, decay, toxicity, provenance and processing history. Flatten nested ledgers without duplicating lots. Conserve all quantities and extensive properties; retain heterogeneous properties per lot rather than replacing them with an improved average. A combined supply remains subject to its actual component aging and spoilage.\\nExecution: one active simulation round at 0.5 energy for this bounded operation. Validate and lock source versions at start, reserve them in owner-attributed transaction escrow, and track remainingWork=1. At completion revalidate life, reach, ownership, energy and compatibility; debit energy once and atomically replace source records with one combined record at the actor's accessible location, without changing carried versus ground status or teleporting material. Require all sources to have the same carried/ground disposition; ground sources must be reachable at the chosen output point. Output placement uses shared collision and placement checks, creates no room or blocking structure, and preserves carried load. Failure before commit changes no material. Cancellation, death or invalidation releases original source records at their actual locations with elapsed aging and any already-paid costs preserved; no escrow is cloned or deleted. Expose status and cancel operations and actual remaining work.\\nIntegrate the composite representation with existing inventory and material-reservation consumers, including root-air-drying tray construction. A reservation of ten tenths from fourteen tenths selects stable component slices, transfers their exact mass and provenance into the constructed tray, and leaves four tenths with the corresponding histories. Count each slice only once; never treat a whole combined item as consumed when only part was requested. Preserve all existing tray eligibility, stone, work and energy requirements. Aggregation is not tray construction and creates no tray now.\\nDeclare events material-combine-started, material-combine-completed and material-combine-stopped with actor, operation ID, source/output IDs, component quantities, work, costs and stop reason. Use existing process-progress only if its schema is satisfied. Dependencies are inventory ownership/locking, shared geometry, conservative material splitting and existing crafting reservations. Record code reuse separately from this new aggregation function. Migrate legacy stacks lazily to one-lot ledgers using their actual stored profiles and provenance; preserve IDs until successful commit and do not invent missing history. Implementation, study and use remain separate; review/development advances no simulation time.\",\"experienceReview\":\"This operation resolves a practical supply-addressing obstruction but ordinary stack handling is not, by itself, a pleasurable experience, a new experimentally confirmed finding or sustained meaningful participation. Assign no automatic temporary pleasure or maintained satisfaction for combining, requesting, learning or enabling a later craft. Do not award existing practice sources under an aggregation alias. Any later qualifying performed experience is evaluated by its own registered rules, with health, nutrition and physical comfort remaining independent.\",\"visualReview\":\"Show selected reachable stacks and their quantities before commitment, a one-round handling/progress indicator, and the actual resulting combined supply with expandable component provenance. On success show 1.4 bark units only if validated quantities total fourteen tenths; later reservation should visibly show 1.0 transferred and 0.4 remaining. Replay the declared operation events with actual locations, paid energy, ledger changes and cancellation state. Do not show a completed tray, improved material quality or a happiness effect merely from combining.\",\"learning\":1}]}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}}

